# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles MUST keep LF endings.
#
# Git's autocrlf on Windows was rewriting scripts/*.sh to CRLF, which makes bash
# fail with `syntax error near unexpected token $'in\r'` — and the same file
# then breaks inside a Linux container, where every one of these actually runs.
# The compat checker caught it; without this line it would come back on the next
# fresh clone.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
